{"parentUuid":"29df50b6-81ca-4913-84d9-7a8a5406662c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZjqwBXUgRASD36jvsWo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017txo1W3aBzgnoooBqkShMJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/levels.md <<'EOF'\n\n## A5\n\n| Spike | Result | Date | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N8 | pass | 2026-10-31 | A `harness::hook::pre-trigger` binding answers `{ \"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": … }` or `{ \"decision\": \"hold\", … }`. A denied call's reason reaches the turn verbatim as its result. A held call parks the turn (status stays `running`), and the envelope carries `session_id`, `turn_id` and `call.id`. `harness::function::resolve` takes `session_id`, `turn_id`, `function_call_id`, `action` (`deliver` or `execute`), `content`, `details` and `is_error`; an unknown field such as `mode` is ignored and the default `deliver` sends an empty result. The held arguments arrive without the hook's `sandbox_id` mutation, so on approval the app runs the call itself, pinned to the job's VM, and delivers the result. `harness::stop` exists and answers `{ \"stopping\": … }`. One run: the model gave up after the deny until told to make the second call anyway. |\nEOF\ncargo +1.97.0 fmt --all && cargo +1.97.0 clippy -p bastion-spikes --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(error|warning)\" | head -3; git add -A && git commit -q -m \"Add spike N8: a hook denies, holds and releases a turn's call\" && git push 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Record N8, lint on 1.97, commit and push","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":856245,"output_tokens":775,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{