{"parentUuid":"c69dcf97-6621-433d-bcc3-2bce6ec82f1b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a1601cc2-bdb1-489e-8288-075aa8dccf5b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017txo1W3aBzgnoooBqkShMJ","type":"tool_result","content":"   853e0bd..e7fb375  main -> main","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dfa430a2-dc16-40a6-82ee-087ffe55ceed","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:12:05.651Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"   853e0bd..e7fb375  main -> main","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"push":{"branch":"main"}},"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-spikes/examples/n8_gate.rs","hunks":[{"oldStart":131,"oldLines":6,"newStart":131,"newLines":12,"lines":["         })","         .await;"," ","-    let _ = call_default(&iii, \"sandbox::stop\", json!({ \"sandbox_id\": box_id, \"wait\": true }), 60_000).await;","+    let _ = call_default(","+        &iii,","+        \"sandbox::stop\",","+        json!({ \"sandbox_id\": box_id, \"wait\": true }),","+        60_000,","+    )","+    .await;","     checks.finish(iii)"," }"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/docs/levels.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":3,"newStart":25,"newLines":9,"lines":[" | Spike | Result | Date | Notes |"," |---|---|---|---|"," | N7 | pass | 2026-10-30 | Two runs, 6.7 s and 5.9 s: `worktree::create` made a worktree of a scratch repo, its branch went into a fresh VM as a git bundle (`sandbox::fs::write` with `content_b64`), one `harness` turn on gpt-5-mini committed there through `sandbox::exec` pinned by the `pre-trigger` hook, and the 377-byte bundle came back through the content channel and fast-forwarded the worktree. `content_b64` is for small files; a large repo needs a channel upload. The spike's cleanup sent the wrong id field to `worktree::remove`, which left one scratch worktree registered. |","+","+## A5","+","+| Spike | Result | Date | Notes |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| N8 | pass | 2026-10-31 | A `harness::hook::pre-trigger` binding answers `{ \"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": … }` or `{ \"decision\": \"hold\", … }`. A denied call's reason reaches the turn verbatim as its result. A held call parks the turn (status stays `running`), and the envelope carries `session_id`, `turn_id` and `call.id`. `harness::function::resolve` takes `session_id`, `turn_id`, `function_call_id`, `action` (`deliver` or `execute`), `content`, `details` and `is_error`; an unknown field such as `mode` is ignored and the default `deliver` sends an empty result. The held arguments arrive without the hook's `sandbox_id` mutation, so on approval the app runs the call itself, pinned to the job's VM, and delivers the result. `harness::stop` exists and answers `{ \"stopping\": … }`. One run: the model gave up after the deny until told to make the second call anyway. |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-spikes/examples/n8_gate.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/docs/levels.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e9279f0b-d7f0-4395-b02b-5a39fa70a266","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c69dcf97-6621-433d-bcc3-2bce6ec82f1b","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dfa430a2-dc16-40a6-82ee-087ffe55ceed","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_017txo1W3aBzgnoooBqkShMJ","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"07d9751f-86ee-4e4a-b421-fefac6817b6c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:12:14.608Z","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"07d9751f-86ee-4e4a-b421-fefac6817b6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZjwz3LnjYsy5PWdkguS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I pushed `mise.toml` and spike N8 as `e7fb375`. CI is green on the earlier fix (`853e0bd`); I haven't checked CI for this push yet.\n\n**`mise.toml`** pins `rust = \"1.97.0\"`. Your terminal will now pick up 1.97 in this repo. My own shell doesn't run mise's hook, so I'll keep checking with `cargo +1.97.0`.\n\n**A5 has started with spike N8, and it passed.** It covers the mechanics the governance layer needs:\n- **Deny:** the hook answers `{ \"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": … }`, and the reason reaches the agent as the call's result, word for word. This is the \"enforced\" rung of a constraint and the \"denied\" rung of a capability.\n- **Hold:** `{ \"decision\": \"hold\" }` parks the call, and the turn waits. This is the \"ask\" rung.\n- **Release:** `harness::function::resolve` takes `session_id`, `turn_id`, `function_call_id`, `action` (`deliver` or `execute`), `content`, `details`, and `is_error`. A held call loses the hook's VM pin, so on approval the app runs the call itself in the job's VM and sends back the result.\n- `harness::stop` exists, so the 60-minute turn cap can now actually stop a turn. Until now a capped turn kept running.\n\n**The rest of A5, in order:**\n1. **Rules in `bastion-core`.** Constraints on the told, checked, enforced ladder. Capabilities on the denied, ask, allowed ladder, per stage. One pure `gate()` function that decides each call, plus the audit hash chain, so the core also gets `sha2` (an update to D19).\n2. **Store tables** for constraints, capabilities, held calls, and audit entries.\n3. **Wiring in the adapter:** the hook calls `gate()`, held calls show on the job page, and every decision is written to the audit chain.\n4. **Pages:** a Constraints page with promote and demote, a Capabilities page, and an Audit page with verify.\n\n**First rules to enforce.** These come straight from what A4 caught agents doing:\n- Never run `bash -lc`.\n- Never delete or overwrite an existing test.\n- Leave a clean tree at the end of a build.\n\nStep 1 adds `sha2` to the core, a dependency beyond what D19 allows today. If you'd rather keep the core to `serde` only, the hashing can live in the adapter instead. Otherwise I'll go ahead with step 1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":857262,"output_tokens":840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":840,"cache_read_input_tokens":857262,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5a2affe3-f122-4b43-a745-2d333a0a3318","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZjwyWbPUD91FtiHWvdq","type":"assistant","uuid":"d6019294-9609-4c23-868f-be577043df78","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:12:14.604Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
