nstraints and\\ncapabilities as hooks on ladders, a tamper-evident audit chain, A/B evals of\\nharness configurations, and integrations as adapters. Reorder the phases so\\ngovernance (A5), evals (A6) and settings and integrations (A7) come next., Guide each turn's tools and flag uncommitted work at review\\n\\nEach turn is told how to reach its VM, that its reply ends the turn, and to run\\nprograms directly with a timeout. The review artifact lists work the turn left\\nuncommitted, which does not land., push, Close A4: land to the workspace's branch, reload pages on focus\\n\\nPass target_branch to worktree::land, show no artifact at a failed land, and\\nread every page again when the window regains focus., Restore the plan's sections 4 to 12 and record A4\\n\\nc963b33 kept only the lines up to the D19 row, so the phases, parity map,\\nrisks and progress table were lost. They are restored with that commit's own\\nedits, and A4 is recorded as done.\\n\\n## Project Rules\\n.claude/CLAUDE.md\\n\\n## Subagent Tasks\\n- [completed] Read-only. Study the repo at /Users/tacoda/Code/wipp (an agentic \\\"software factory\\\" on the iii engine, wi...\\n\\n## Environment\\ncwd: /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion\\nmodel:claude-opus-5-5\\nsed -i '' '129s/, &path, &box_id\\\\[..8\\\\],/, path, \\\\&box_id[..8],/' crates/bastion-spikes/examples/n7_roundtrip.rs && sed -n 129p crates/bastion-spikes/examples/n7_roundtrip.rs; which cargo rustup; rustup toolchain list 2>&1 | head -5\\n\\n## Data References\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- interrupted:false stderrBytes:0\\n- … 126 older captures kept in the sandbox — query mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(source: \\\"session-events\\\").\\n\\n## Session Intent\\nimplement\\n\\n</session_guide>\\n<session_search>\\nDetailed session data is indexed in context-mode FTS5 (source: \\\"session-events\\\").\\nUse mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [...], source: \\\"session-events\\\") when you need specifics.\\nDo NOT call ctx_index() — data is already indexed.\\n</session_search>\\n</session_knowledge>\\n\\n<session_state source=\\\"compaction\\\">\\n\\n<rules>\\nFollow these decisions:\\n- yes, commit, and push\\nThen start on A0\\n- I want to pivot from inbox and floor\\nThe main idea should be the job - that's the request or the tic\\n- The main benefit that bastion provides is providing constraints and capabilities, a way to promote a\\n- This app should be general and allow you to configure all of your settings and accounts to use the p\\n- screen is free, finish the A4 exit\\n</rules>\\n\\n<session_mode>implement</session_mode>\\n\\n</session_state>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":88},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2f085a93-7a35-4795-a1e4-b08c11dd8ddd","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:14:17.446Z","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"2f085a93-7a35-4795-a1e4-b08c11dd8ddd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (32.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48/tool-results/hook-898cdcca-02f7-495d-9aa0-12ebc9f08bd9-7-additionalContext.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n\n<context_window_protection>\n  <priority_instructions>\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\n  </priority_instructions>\n\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \"timeline\")\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\n       - Each command: {label: \"section header\", command: \"shell command\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\"q1\", \"q2\", ...])\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\n\n  <when_not_to_use>\n...\n</persisted-output>"],"hookName":"SessionStart","toolUseID":"SessionStart","hookEvent":"SessionStart"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7b281260-3857-4a69-8f1d-e08757593cf3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:14:17.447Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nSessionStart hook additional context: <persisted-output>\nOutput too large (32.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48/tool-results/hook-898cdcca-02f7-495d-9aa0-12ebc9f08bd9-7-additionalContext.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n\n<context_window_protection>\n  <priority_instructions>\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\n  </priority_instructions>\n\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \"timeline\")\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\n       - Each command: {label: \"section header\", command: \"shell command\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\"q1\", \"q2\", ...])\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\n\n  <when_not_to_use>\n...\n</persisted-output>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
