{"parentUuid":"a5d6a700-0bea-4ba2-b992-4703c7dcbc5f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01KXqDPzzm6JRH24vJajUctk","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":58},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a1dd6b66-32fb-4e20-aa12-1e93f4fee8f6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:15:53.591Z","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"a5d6a700-0bea-4ba2-b992-4703c7dcbc5f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4ff2de2d-1928-42ed-8fcf-65f2b442b6fc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KXqDPzzm6JRH24vJajUctk","type":"tool_result","content":"//! The factory's rules (PLAN.md D18, §6.1). Everything here is a pure\n//! function: an event and the current job go in, the next job and the effects\n//! to run come out. No I/O, no clock, no engine.\n\nmod brief;\n\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\npub use brief::{QUESTION_MARKER, brief, outcome};\n\n/// How many failed turns in a row a stage gets before the job fails (D16).\npub const MAX_TURN_FAILURES: u32 = 2;\n/// The longest a turn may run before it counts as failed (PLAN.md §9).\n// ponytail: one cap for every stage; give each stage its own when a stage needs longer.\npub const TURN_CAP_SECS: u64 = 60 * 60;\n\n/// The stages of the short pipeline (D17), in order.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum Stage {\n    /// An agent reads the code and writes a plan.\n    Plan,\n    /// The owner approves the plan, or comments on it.\n    Approve,\n    /// An agent carries the plan out.\n    Build,\n    /// The owner approves the change, or comments on it.\n    Review,\n    /// The change lands on the workspace's branch.\n    Land,\n}\n\npub const SHORT_PIPELINE: [Stage; 5] = [\n    Stage::Plan,\n    Stage::Approve,\n    Stage::Build,\n    Stage::Review,\n    Stage::Land,\n];\n\nimpl Stage {\n    /// The checkpoint a person decides, if this stage is one.\n    pub fn is_checkpoint(self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Stage::Approve | Stage::Review)\n    }\n\n    /// An agent stage may not change the tree.\n    pub fn read_only(self) -> bool {\n        self == Stage::Plan\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum State {\n    /// Waiting for a free sandbox.\n    Queued,\n    /// Getting its worktree and VM.\n    Provisioning,\n    /// An agent turn is running.\n    Running,\n    /// A checkpoint or a question waits on the owner.\n    NeedsYou,\n    Landed,\n    Failed,\n    Stopped,\n}\n\nimpl State {\n    pub fn finished(self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, State::Landed | State::Failed | State::Stopped)\n    }\n\n    /// Holds a sandbox VM.\n    pub fn holds_vm(self) -> bool {\n        !self.finished() && self != State::Queued\n    }\n}\n\n/// One request against one workspace, and where it is in its pipeline.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct Job {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub workspace: String,\n    pub request: String,\n    pub stage: Stage,\n    pub state: State,\n    /// What the owner must answer while `NeedsYou` holds outside a checkpoint.\n    pub question: Option<String>,\n    /// The note that becomes the next turn's brief (D16).\n    pub feedback: Option<String>,\n    /// The latest plan the agent wrote, carried into the build brief.\n    pub plan: Option<String>,\n    pub failures: u32,\n    /// Why the job failed, when it did.\n    pub error: Option<String>,\n    pub updated_at: u64,\n}\n\n/// Something that happened to a job.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\", tag = \"kind\")]\npub enum Event {\n    /// A sandbox is free for this queued job.\n    Admitted,\n    Provisioned,\n    ProvisionFailed {\n        error: String,\n    },\n    TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome,\n    },\n    /// The owner approved the checkpoint the job waits at.\n    Approved,\n    /// The owner commented on the artifact at the checkpoint, or answered a question.\n    Commented {\n        text: String,\n    },\n    Landed,\n    LandFailed {\n        error: String,\n    },\n    Stopped,\n    /// A held checkpoint's time ran out (D15).\n    HoldExpired {\n        stage: Stage,\n    },\n}\n\n/// How a checkpoint is decided (D15): the owner decides, the default lands\n/// after a hold unless the owner acts first, or the default lands at once.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum Dial {\n    #[default]\n    Ask,\n    Hold,\n    Auto,\n}\n\n5:mod brief;\n9:pub use brief::{QUESTION_MARKER, brief, outcome};\n12:pub const MAX_TURN_FAILURES: u32 = 2;\n15:pub const TURN_CAP_SECS: u64 = 60 * 60;\n20:pub enum Stage {\n33:pub const SHORT_PIPELINE: [Stage; 5] = [\n55:pub enum State {\n82:pub struct Job {\n103:pub enum Event {\n134:pub enum Dial {\n142:pub const HOLD_SECS: u64 = 30 * 60;\n146:pub struct Dials {\n167:pub enum Outcome {\n180:pub enum Effect {\n221:pub fn step(job: &Job, event: &Event, at: u64, dials: &Dials) -> (Job, Vec<Effect>) {\n371:pub enum StepState {\n385:pub fn steps(job: &Job) -> Vec<(Stage, StepState)> {\n412:pub fn hold_until(job: &Job, dials: &Dials) -> Option<u64> {\n420:pub enum Action {\n430:pub fn actions(job: &Job) -> Vec<Action> {\n449:pub fn admit(jobs: &[Job], limit: usize) -> Vec<String> {\n460:#[cfg(test)]\n461:mod tests;\n//! Every transition of the short pipeline, as plain function calls.\n\nuse super::*;\n\nconst AT: u64 = 1_000;\n\nfn job() -> Job {\n    Job::new(\n        \"j1\".into(),\n        \"bastion\".into(),\n        \"Add a health check\".into(),\n        AT,\n    )\n}\n\nfn done(report: &str) -> Event {\n    Event::TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome::Done {\n            report: report.into(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\nfn failed() -> Event {\n    Event::TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome::Failed {\n            error: \"timeout\".into(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\n/// Run events in order, and return the job and the last step's effects.\nfn run(events: &[Event]) -> (Job, Vec<Effect>) {\n    let mut current = (job(), Vec::new());\n    for (i, e) in events.iter().enumerate() {\n        current = step(&current.0, e, AT + 1 + i as u64, &Dials::default());\n    }\n    current\n}\n\n29:## A5\n30-\n31-| Spike | Result | Date | Notes |\n32-|---|---|---|---|\n33-| N8 | pass | 2026-10-31 | A `harness::hook::pre-trigger` binding answers `{ \"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": … }` or `{ \"decision\": \"hold\", … }`. A denied call's reason reaches the turn verbatim as its result. A held call parks the turn (status stays `running`), and the envelope carries `session_id`, `turn_id` and `call.id`. `harness::function::resolve` takes `session_id`, `turn_id`, `function_call_id`, `action` (`deliver` or `execute`), `content`, `details` and `is_error`; an unknown field such as `mode` is ignored and the default `deliver` sends an empty result. The held arguments arrive without the hook's `sandbox_id` mutation, so on approval the app runs the call itself, pinned to the job's VM, and delivers the result. `harness::stop` exists and answers `{ \"stopping\": … }`. One run: the model gave up after the deny until told to make the second call anyway. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d82251d4-ce9e-4bf9-a7d0-d85cc63acf0c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:15:54.104Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"//! The factory's rules (PLAN.md D18, §6.1). Everything here is a pure\n//! function: an event and the current job go in, the next job and the effects\n//! to run come out. No I/O, no clock, no engine.\n\nmod brief;\n\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\npub use brief::{QUESTION_MARKER, brief, outcome};\n\n/// How many failed turns in a row a stage gets before the job fails (D16).\npub const MAX_TURN_FAILURES: u32 = 2;\n/// The longest a turn may run before it counts as failed (PLAN.md §9).\n// ponytail: one cap for every stage; give each stage its own when a stage needs longer.\npub const TURN_CAP_SECS: u64 = 60 * 60;\n\n/// The stages of the short pipeline (D17), in order.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum Stage {\n    /// An agent reads the code and writes a plan.\n    Plan,\n    /// The owner approves the plan, or comments on it.\n    Approve,\n    /// An agent carries the plan out.\n    Build,\n    /// The owner approves the change, or comments on it.\n    Review,\n    /// The change lands on the workspace's branch.\n    Land,\n}\n\npub const SHORT_PIPELINE: [Stage; 5] = [\n    Stage::Plan,\n    Stage::Approve,\n    Stage::Build,\n    Stage::Review,\n    Stage::Land,\n];\n\nimpl Stage {\n    /// The checkpoint a person decides, if this stage is one.\n    pub fn is_checkpoint(self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Stage::Approve | Stage::Review)\n    }\n\n    /// An agent stage may not change the tree.\n    pub fn read_only(self) -> bool {\n        self == Stage::Plan\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum State {\n    /// Waiting for a free sandbox.\n    Queued,\n    /// Getting its worktree and VM.\n    Provisioning,\n    /// An agent turn is running.\n    Running,\n    /// A checkpoint or a question waits on the owner.\n    NeedsYou,\n    Landed,\n    Failed,\n    Stopped,\n}\n\nimpl State {\n    pub fn finished(self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, State::Landed | State::Failed | State::Stopped)\n    }\n\n    /// Holds a sandbox VM.\n    pub fn holds_vm(self) -> bool {\n        !self.finished() && self != State::Queued\n    }\n}\n\n/// One request against one workspace, and where it is in its pipeline.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct Job {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub workspace: String,\n    pub request: String,\n    pub stage: Stage,\n    pub state: State,\n    /// What the owner must answer while `NeedsYou` holds outside a checkpoint.\n    pub question: Option<String>,\n    /// The note that becomes the next turn's brief (D16).\n    pub feedback: Option<String>,\n    /// The latest plan the agent wrote, carried into the build brief.\n    pub plan: Option<String>,\n    pub failures: u32,\n    /// Why the job failed, when it did.\n    pub error: Option<String>,\n    pub updated_at: u64,\n}\n\n/// Something that happened to a job.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\", tag = \"kind\")]\npub enum Event {\n    /// A sandbox is free for this queued job.\n    Admitted,\n    Provisioned,\n    ProvisionFailed {\n        error: String,\n    },\n    TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome,\n    },\n    /// The owner approved the checkpoint the job waits at.\n    Approved,\n    /// The owner commented on the artifact at the checkpoint, or answered a question.\n    Commented {\n        text: String,\n    },\n    Landed,\n    LandFailed {\n        error: String,\n    },\n    Stopped,\n    /// A held checkpoint's time ran out (D15).\n    HoldExpired {\n        stage: Stage,\n    },\n}\n\n/// How a checkpoint is decided (D15): the owner decides, the default lands\n/// after a hold unless the owner acts first, or the default lands at once.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum Dial {\n    #[default]\n    Ask,\n    Hold,\n    Auto,\n}\n\n5:mod brief;\n9:pub use brief::{QUESTION_MARKER, brief, outcome};\n12:pub const MAX_TURN_FAILURES: u32 = 2;\n15:pub const TURN_CAP_SECS: u64 = 60 * 60;\n20:pub enum Stage {\n33:pub const SHORT_PIPELINE: [Stage; 5] = [\n55:pub enum State {\n82:pub struct Job {\n103:pub enum Event {\n134:pub enum Dial {\n142:pub const HOLD_SECS: u64 = 30 * 60;\n146:pub struct Dials {\n167:pub enum Outcome {\n180:pub enum Effect {\n221:pub fn step(job: &Job, event: &Event, at: u64, dials: &Dials) -> (Job, Vec<Effect>) {\n371:pub enum StepState {\n385:pub fn steps(job: &Job) -> Vec<(Stage, StepState)> {\n412:pub fn hold_until(job: &Job, dials: &Dials) -> Option<u64> {\n420:pub enum Action {\n430:pub fn actions(job: &Job) -> Vec<Action> {\n449:pub fn admit(jobs: &[Job], limit: usize) -> Vec<String> {\n460:#[cfg(test)]\n461:mod tests;\n//! Every transition of the short pipeline, as plain function calls.\n\nuse super::*;\n\nconst AT: u64 = 1_000;\n\nfn job() -> Job {\n    Job::new(\n        \"j1\".into(),\n        \"bastion\".into(),\n        \"Add a health check\".into(),\n        AT,\n    )\n}\n\nfn done(report: &str) -> Event {\n    Event::TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome::Done {\n            report: report.into(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\nfn failed() -> Event {\n    Event::TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome::Failed {\n            error: \"timeout\".into(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\n/// Run events in order, and return the job and the last step's effects.\nfn run(events: &[Event]) -> (Job, Vec<Effect>) {\n    let mut current = (job(), Vec::new());\n    for (i, e) in events.iter().enumerate() {\n        current = step(&current.0, e, AT + 1 + i as u64, &Dials::default());\n    }\n    current\n}\n\n29:## A5\n30-\n31-| Spike | Result | Date | Notes |\n32-|---|---|---|---|\n33-| N8 | pass | 2026-10-31 | A `harness::hook::pre-trigger` binding answers `{ \"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": … }` or `{ \"decision\": \"hold\", … }`. A denied call's reason reaches the turn verbatim as its result. A held call parks the turn (status stays `running`), and the envelope carries `session_id`, `turn_id` and `call.id`. `harness::function::resolve` takes `session_id`, `turn_id`, `function_call_id`, `action` (`deliver` or `execute`), `content`, `details` and `is_error`; an unknown field such as `mode` is ignored and the default `deliver` sends an empty result. The held arguments arrive without the hook's `sandbox_id` mutation, so on approval the app runs the call itself, pinned to the job's VM, and delivers the result. `harness::stop` exists and answers `{ \"stopping\": … }`. One run: the model gave up after the deny until told to make the second call anyway. |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifier