{"parentUuid":"89afa50c-a011-4122-83c8-4770de47ccea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZkGMPjBz1J64VVudczx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Updating PLAN.md for A5 progress and the `sha2` change to D19, then writing the gate and audit chain in `bastion-core`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":91532,"output_tokens":806,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":91532,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"35637123-f6e3-4df7-bd89-c6cac3fc5270","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZkGMALjFAsTtsgNC4Q5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fab2fff-8a69-4b68-b308-646cead37bd6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:16:16.239Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"6fab2fff-8a69-4b68-b308-646cead37bd6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZkGMPjBz1J64VVudczx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U2rz5ahimkjWFt6GpNKW2P","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read(); n=len(s)\nreps=[\n(\"gains a dependency other than `serde`, or if\",\"gains a dependency other than `serde`, or if `bastion-core` gains one other than `serde` and `sha2` (for the audit chain, D21), or if\"),\n(\"bastion-core       ──>  serde only\",\"bastion-core       ──>  serde, sha2 (the audit chain, D21)\"),\n(\"| A5 | next | — |\",\"| A5 | in progress | Spike N8 passes: a hook denies, holds and releases a call (e7fb375). `mise.toml` pins Rust 1.97 so local checks match CI (c8c6518). Step 1, the rules in `bastion-core`: constraint and capability ladders, the gate, and the audit chain. Next: the Store tables, the hook wired to the gate, held calls on the job page, and the Constraints, Capabilities and Audit pages. |\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\"\"\n\n**What A5 found so far:**\n\n- A `pre-trigger` hook answers `continue`, `deny` with a `reason`, or `hold`.\n  The deny reason reaches the turn as the call's result, word for word (N8).\n- A held call arrives without the hook's `sandbox_id` pin. On approval the app\n  runs the call itself in the job's VM and sends the result back with\n  `harness::function::resolve` (`action: \"deliver\"`).\n- `harness::stop` exists, so the turn cap can stop a turn, which A4 thought it\n  could not.\n- `bastion-core` takes `sha2` for the audit chain. The hash is part of the\n  rule, so it stays pure and tested with the rest (D19 updated).\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print(n,len(s))\nEOF\ntail -5 PLAN.md","description":"Update plan progress, D19 and A5 notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":91532,"output_tokens":806,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":91532,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01U2rz5ahimkjWFt6GpNKW2P":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read(); n=len(s)\nreps=[\n(\"gains a dependency other than `serde`, or if\",\"gains a dependency other than `serde`, or if `bastion-core` gains one other than `serde` and `sha2` (for the audit chain, D21), or if\"),\n(\"bastion-core       ──>  serde only\",\"bastion-core       ──>  serde, sha2 (the audit chain, D21)\"),\n(\"| A5 | next | — |\",\"| A5 | in progress | Spike N8 passes: a hook denies, holds and releases a call (e7fb375). `mise.toml` pins Rust 1.97 so local checks match CI (c8c6518). Step 1, the rules in `bastion-core`: constraint and capability ladders, the gate, and the audit chain. Next: the Store tables, the hook wired to the gate, held calls on the job page, and the Constraints, Capabilities and Audit pages. |\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\"\"\n\n**What A5 found so far:**\n\n- A `pre-trigger` hook answers `continue`, `deny` with a `reason`, or `hold`.\n  The deny reason reaches the turn as the call's result, word for word (N8).\n- A held call arrives without the hook's `sandbox_id` pin. On approval the app\n  runs the call itself in the job's VM and sends the result back with\n  `harness::function::resolve` (`action: \"deliver\"`).\n- `harness::stop` exists, so the turn cap can stop a turn, which A4 thought it\n  could not.\n- `bastion-core` takes `sha2` for the audit chain. The hash is part of the\n  rule, so it stays pure and tested with the rest (D19 updated).\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print(n,len(s))\nEOF\ntail -5 PLAN.md","description":"Update plan progress, D19 and A5 notes"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01U2rz5ahimkjWFt6GpNKW2P":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"35637123-f6e3-4df7-bd89-c6cac3fc5270","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZkGMALjFAsTtsgNC4Q5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b27d7b4-bb3d-47a3-998a-7c8d73d76abe","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:16:22.177Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
