{"parentUuid":"3c9a3bd1-85fe-4901-935f-bd7c0ba5ef37","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaX1w9KYh5qMFNTLkaHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":232441,"output_tokens":1166,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":232441,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f6a2934d-3daf-4ef9-bb1f-a4be73545c02","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgaX1vbpxsDX7Fu2iLUcD","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9a276af-dcb7-452a-bf2d-269029f57396","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:03:14.466Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"b9a276af-dcb7-452a-bf2d-269029f57396","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaX1w9KYh5qMFNTLkaHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've updated the plan and finished A5 steps 1 to 4. All four are pushed: `def679b`, `a509bb1` and `b4f2704`. CI was not checked on any of them. Locally, fmt, the seam check, clippy (app and view) and all tests pass: 37 core, 39 app and 1 view.\n\n**Security issue, please check this first.** In the process list, the `opengantry` worker VM received the whole environment of the shell that started the stack as `--env` flags. That includes several API keys, GitHub and npm tokens, Jira credentials and passwords. Anything that runs in that VM can read them. The values also passed through my context when I listed processes; I have not repeated them anywhere. Before any real work runs in the VM, start the stack from a clean environment that holds only the keys the stack needs, and consider rotating the tokens that leaked. In A9, Bastion should pass the stack only an allowlist of variables.\n\n**What's built:**\n- **The rules, in `bastion-core`:** constraints on the told, checked, enforced ladder. Capabilities on the denied, ask, allowed ladder, per stage. A pure `gate()` function decides each call. The audit chain is hashed with `sha2`, and D19 and the seam check now allow that dependency.\n- **The store:** four new tables for constraints, capabilities, held calls and the audit chain. The owner's default rules are seeded once, and a rung the owner changed is kept. An audit entry's number is the table key, so two writers can't fork the chain.\n- **The hook:** every `sandbox::*` call now goes through the gate. The hook reads the rules from memory, and one background task writes holds and audit entries, so a slow store can't stall a turn. A call the gate can't judge is refused.\n- **Owner actions:**\n  - \"Allow once\" runs the held call itself in the job's VM and sends back the result.\n  - \"Refuse\" sends the owner's note back to the agent as an error.\n  - Stopping a job clears its held calls.\n  - Promote and demote take effect at once and are recorded in the audit chain.\n  - Every rule goes into the turn's brief.\n- **Pages:** the job page lists held calls. A new Governance page shows constraints, capabilities and the audit chain, verified each time it loads. I put all three on one page rather than three; say if you want them split.\n\n**Not built yet:** constraints taken from a workspace's charter, repository hooks, audit export, and the audit timeout test.\n\n**A live test failed to run.** The two store tests that need the stack hung waiting for the engine link, even though port 49160 answers. The governance SQL had passed live earlier in this session, before I split it into its own test, so the hang looks like the link, not the queries. I haven't found the cause.\n\n**Next is the A5 live exit, and it needs your screen.** I'll drive the window and run a few short turns on gpt-5-mini, at a few cents each. The exit checks four things:\n1. A plan turn's file write waits on the job page.\n2. \"Allow once\" lets exactly that call through, and the next write waits again.\n3. Promoting `keep-tests` to enforced makes a `git rm` call get refused.\n4. The audit chain verifies, then fails after I change one byte in it.\n\nTell me when the screen is free."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":232441,"output_tokens":1166,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":232441,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f6a2934d-3daf-4ef9-bb1f-a4be73545c02","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgaX1vbpxsDX7Fu2iLUcD","type":"assistant","uuid":"2dce54c3-de4b-4ba8-911f-861b61247b28","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:03:18.080Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
