{"parentUuid":"99026fa1-4461-4bc3-a070-38189c15a625","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"50b0f09b-314b-4bce-88c1-683a5cd802dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011N9oZcctUsuhB7bA1JXQtn","type":"tool_result","content":"70\tpub struct Constraint {\n71\t    pub id: String,\n72\t    /// What the agent is told.\n73\t    pub rule: String,\n74\t    /// The calls it binds: a function pattern (see [`matches`]) and text the\n75\t    /// call contains. An empty pattern binds no call, so the rule can only be\n76\t    /// told.\n77\t    pub function: String,\n78\t    pub contains: String,\n79\t    pub rung: Enforcement,\n80\t    pub source: Source,\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\t/// A grant: what calls to a function pattern may do at one stage.\n84\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n85\tpub struct Capability {\n86\t    pub stage: Stage,\n87\t    pub function: String,\n88\t    pub rung: Access,\n89\t}\n90\t\n91\t/// One call a turn makes. `text` is its arguments as the rules read them,\n92\t/// such as a command line or a path.\n93\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n94\tpub struct Call {\n95\t    pub function: String,\n96\t    pub text: String,\n97\t}\n98\t\n99\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n100\t#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\", tag = \"decision\")]\n101\tpub enum Decision {\n102\t    Continue,\n103\t    Deny {\n104\t        reason: String,\n105\t    },\n106\t    /// Wait for the owner: retry with feedback, allow this call once, or stop.\n107\t    Hold {\n108\t        reason: String,\n109\t    },\n110\t}\n111\t\n112\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n113\tpub struct Verdict {\n114\t    pub decision: Decision,\n115\t    /// The constraints at `checked` that the call breaks, for the record.\n116\t    pub flagged: Vec<String>,\n117\t}\n118\t\n119\t/// `name` matches a pattern that equals it, or a pattern ending in `*` that\n120\t/// it starts with. The empty pattern matches nothing.\n121\tpub fn matches(pattern: &str, name: &str) -> bool {\n122\t    match pattern.strip_suffix('*') {\n123\t        Some(prefix) => !pattern.is_empty() && name.starts_with(prefix),\n124\t        None => !pattern.is_empty() && pattern == name,\n125\t    }\n126\t}\n127\t\n128\t/// Judge one call. An enforced constraint refuses it first. Then the most\n129\t/// specific grant for the stage decides, and a call no grant covers is\n130\t/// refused.\n131\tpub fn gate(\n132\t    call: &Call,\n133\t    stage: Stage,\n134\t    constraints: &[Constraint],\n135\t    grants: &[Capability],\n136\t) -> Verdict {\n137\t    let broken = || {\n138\t        constraints\n139\t            .iter()\n140\t            .filter(|c| matches(&c.function, &call.function) && call.text.contains(&c.contains))\n141\t    };\n142\t    let flagged = broken()\n143\t        .filter(|c| c.rung == Enforcement::Checked)\n144\t        .map(|c| c.id.clone())"}]},"uuid":"d17b5743-6fb0-45a4-afe9-b9cea720248e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:14:24.411Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs","content":"pub struct Constraint {\n    pub id: String,\n    /// What the agent is told.\n    pub rule: String,\n    /// The calls it binds: a function pattern (see [`matches`]) and text the\n    /// call contains. An empty pattern binds no call, so the rule can only be\n    /// told.\n    pub function: String,\n    pub contains: String,\n    pub rung: Enforcement,\n    pub source: Source,\n}\n\n/// A grant: what calls to a function pattern may do at one stage.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct Capability {\n    pub stage: Stage,\n    pub function: String,\n    pub rung: Access,\n}\n\n/// One call a turn makes. `text` is its arguments as the rules read them,\n/// such as a command line or a path.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct Call {\n    pub function: String,\n    pub text: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\", tag = \"decision\")]\npub enum Decision {\n    Continue,\n    Deny {\n        reason: String,\n    },\n    /// Wait for the owner: retry with feedback, allow this call once, or stop.\n    Hold {\n        reason: String,\n    },\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct Verdict {\n    pub decision: Decision,\n    /// The constraints at `checked` that the call breaks, for the record.\n    pub flagged: Vec<String>,\n}\n\n/// `name` matches a pattern that equals it, or a pattern ending in `*` that\n/// it starts with. The empty pattern matches nothing.\npub fn matches(pattern: &str, name: &str) -> bool {\n    match pattern.strip_suffix('*') {\n        Some(prefix) => !pattern.is_empty() && name.starts_with(prefix),\n        None => !pattern.is_empty() && pattern == name,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Judge one call. An enforced constraint refuses it first. Then the most\n/// specific grant for the stage decides, and a call no grant covers is\n/// refused.\npub fn gate(\n    call: &Call,\n    stage: Stage,\n    constraints: &[Constraint],\n    grants: &[Capability],\n) -> Verdict {\n    let broken = || {\n        constraints\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|c| matches(&c.function, &call.function) && call.text.contains(&c.contains))\n    };\n    let flagged = broken()\n        .filter(|c| c.rung == Enforcement::Checked)\n        .map(|c| c.id.clone())","numLines":75,"startLine":70,"totalLines":370}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"99026fa1-4461-4bc3-a070-38189c15a625","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
